WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.136
A second model as checker, and why it is not a referee.

2
00:00:03.416 --> 00:00:09.517
Item 2 from the exercise needs judgment: does this quote show this person committing to this task?

3
00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:19.781
A natural tool is a second model call that receives the transcript, one item, and a narrow question (“Does the evidence show the named owner committing to the task?

4
00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:22.792
Answer yes, no, or unclear, with the reason”).

5
00:00:23.072 --> 00:00:25.205
This is the LLM-as-judge pattern.

6
00:00:25.485 --> 00:00:33.784
Making the question narrow and binary, about one item at a time, is far more reliable than asking a model to “review the extraction.

7
00:00:34.064 --> 00:00:34.362
”.

8
00:00:34.642 --> 00:00:36.754
Know its limits before you rely on it.

9
00:00:37.034 --> 00:00:55.764
Zheng and colleagues (2023) found that strong judge models agreed with human preferences over 80 percent of the time, about as often as humans agree with each other, but also documented position bias, verbosity bias, and self-enhancement bias (favoring answers like their own),

10
00:00:56.044 --> 00:00:58.519
plus limited reasoning on hard questions.

11
00:00:58.799 --> 00:01:09.018
Self-enhancement is the reason to consider a checker from a different model family than the extractor: errors that come from the same training are more likely to be shared.

12
00:01:09.298 --> 00:01:18.087
A Claude extractor checked by a GPT or Gemini model (or the reverse) gives you more independent errors, though not independent ones.

13
00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:22.058
Above all, a checker is another model output that needs checking.

14
00:01:22.338 --> 00:01:39.639
Hamel Husain’s practical guide to LLM judges describes the discipline: label a set of examples yourself, treat those human labels as ground truth, and measure the judge’s true positive and true negative rates separately rather than one overall agreement number,

15
00:01:39.919 --> 00:01:43.311
because raw agreement misleads when most items are fine.

16
00:01:43.591 --> 00:01:48.348
If the checker misses half the bad items, it is a speed bump, not a safety net.
